we can put the resource in try block which can implement the autocloseable interface.


Resources like FileReader,FileWriter,..etc. utilizes system resources.once the operation is completed that resource must be released.
To release these resources we need to call close() method in each of the resources.

Generally we call the close() in the finally block to make sure that the resources is closed regarless of an exception.

we csn even avoid calling close() method explicitily in finally block.
TO avoid calling close() method explicitly.
we need to use try with resources.

try with resources has a seprate syntax,try followed with braces. Inside these braces we need create the resources for eg: Filewriter

When the resource is kept inside these braces,
try with resource will automatically close the resource.
we donnot have to call close() method explicitly.

The resources which are kept inside try with resource brackets,must implements autocloseable interface.

The resource implementing Autoclosable will be automatically closed.
This avoids the resource leakage problem in the application.

Resource leakage means when a program opens I/O streams like FileWriter,FileReader,Connection Statement ,scanner ... etc.
but fails to close it after use,the system resources like file handles and memory will remaining occupied.

This is called Resource leakage.



